I did not add the two operations-team requests (the log file and the metadata fetch). This node's world grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, so it has no filesystem or HTTP import, and there is no `wasm32-unknown-unknown` path to either. Adding `http-client` or a file capability would widen the node's authority beyond its declared contract. If operations needs them, they should be granted in the graph as separate capabilities.

The store has no way to list keys, so the node reads the key `subscriptions`. I assumed the stored value is newline-separated URLs, which is also an assumption, since the spec doesn't say.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let urls = match state_read::get("subscriptions") {
            Some(raw) => raw
                .lines()
                .map(|l| l.trim())
                .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
                .map(|l| l.to_string())
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };
        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

